MMMMM----- Recipe via Meal-Master (from JavaRecipes)

      Title: Rice Croquettes with Ham and Mozzarella
 Categories: Rice
      Yield: 0 Servings

      4 Beef stock
      2 Unsalted butter
  1 1/2 Arborio Rice
    1/2  c Tomato sauce
    1/2  c Parmesan cheese -- grated
      1 Salt & pepper -- as required
      1 lg Egg yolk -- beaten
      1 sl Smoked Ham -- diced
      3 oz Fresh mozzarella cheese -- di
           - ced
    1/2  c Peas -- boiled 1 min & draine
           - d
  2 1/2  c Bread crumbs
      1 pk Peanut oil -- for deep Frying

Pour the stock into a saucepan and bring it to a simmer.

Melt the butter in a second pan. Add the rice and stir to coat.

Remove from the heat and stir in the tomato sauce and cheese.

Shape into balls, coat with crumbs and fry in hot oil. Serve immediately.

Source:
  "Example Cookbook"
Notes:
  "Any stock works in place of the beef stock"
Yield:
  6 Servings"
S("Cuisine")
  "Italian"

